Feature: The master-main reconcile refuses only when git itself would refuse

  # BL-919. BL-891's sweep gates on `git status --porcelain` being wholly
  # blank, so any dirt at all blocks reconciliation - including dirt git
  # would never touch. Parked as .feature.draft (BL-233): these scenarios
  # describe a Babashka daemon sweep the JS acceptance runner cannot bind.
  # The live gate is the unit suite under swarmforge/scripts/test/.

  Background:
    Given a master checkout whose local main is behind origin/main

  # BL-919 dirt-clear-of-the-merge-reconciles-01
  Scenario: dirt that the merge would not touch does not block it
    Given the working tree has uncommitted changes
    And none of those paths is one the incoming merge would change
    When the reconcile sweep runs
    Then local main is reconciled with origin/main
    And every uncommitted change is left exactly as it was

  # BL-919 dirt-overlapping-the-merge-refuses-02
  Scenario: dirt on a path the merge would change still blocks
    Given the working tree has uncommitted changes
    And at least one of those paths is one the incoming merge would change
    When the reconcile sweep runs
    Then no merge is attempted
    And the block is surfaced with the paths that caused it

  # BL-919 untracked-clash-refuses-03
  Scenario: an untracked file the merge would create still blocks
    Given the working tree holds an untracked file
    And the incoming merge would create a file at that same path
    When the reconcile sweep runs
    Then no merge is attempted
    And the block is surfaced with the paths that caused it

  # BL-919 clean-tree-unchanged-04
  Scenario: a clean tree reconciles exactly as it did before
    Given the working tree is clean
    When the reconcile sweep runs
    Then local main is reconciled with origin/main

  # BL-919 conflict-still-aborts-05
  Scenario: a real conflict is still aborted, never left mid-merge
    Given the working tree has no dirt on any path the merge would change
    And the incoming merge conflicts with local-only commits
    When the reconcile sweep runs
    Then the merge is aborted
    And the checkout is left exactly as the sweep found it

  # BL-919 never-stash-reset-rebase-force-06
  Scenario: the sweep never rewrites or sets aside local work
    Given any working tree state
    When the reconcile sweep runs
    Then it never stashes, resets, rebases, or force-updates
    And every commit reachable before the sweep is still reachable after
